{"groups":[[["Bojjhaṃga sutta","The Discourse on the Factors of Enlightenment"]],[["Saṃsāre saṃsarantānaṃ","For those wandering in the cycle of rebirth,"],["Sabba dukkha vināsane","destroying all suffering,"],["Sattadhammeca bojjhaṃge","the seven factors of enlightenment,"],["Mārasenāpamaddane","and crushing the army of Mara;"]],[["Khujjhitvā ye pime satte","Whichever beings, having understood these (factors),"],["Tihavā muttakuttamā","the supreme ones freed from the three worlds of existence,"],["Ajātiṃ ajarābyādhiṃ","to the birthless, ageless, disease-free,"],["Amataṃ nibbhayaṃ gatā","and fearless state of the deathless (Nirvana) have gone."]],[["Evamādī guṇopetaṃ","Endowed with such and other qualities,"],["Aneka guṇasaṃgahaṃ","a collection of manifold virtues,"],["Osadhaṃ ca imaṃ mantaṃ","this medicine and this mantra,"],["Bojjhaṃgaṃ ca bhaṇāmahe","we now recite this Bojjhanga (Paritta)."]],[["Bojjhaṃgo sati saṃkhāto","The enlightenment factor of mindfulness,"],["Dhammānaṃ vicayo tathā","likewise the investigation of phenomena,"],["Viriyaṃ pīti passaddhi","energy, rapture, and tranquility,"],["Bojjhaṃgā ca tato pare","are the subsequent factors of enlightenment."]],[["Samādhupekkhā bojjhaṃgā","The enlightenment factors of concentration and equanimity,"],["Satte te sabbadassinā,","these seven, by the All-Seeing"],["Muninā sammadakkhātā","Sage, have been perfectly expounded,"],["Bhāvitā bahulīkatā","cultivated and frequently practiced."]],[["Saṃvattanti abhiññāya","They lead to profound knowledge,"],["Nibbāṇāya ca bodhiyā,","to realization (of Nirvana) and to enlightenment."],["Etena sacca vajjena","By the speaking of this truth,"],["Sotthi (te) hotu sabbadā","may you always be well!"]],[["Ekasmiṃ samaye nātho","On one occasion, the Protector (the Buddha),"],["Moggallānañca kassapaṃ,","seeing Venerable Moggallana and Kassapa,"],["Gilāne dukkhite disvā","sick and suffering,"],["Bojjhaṃge satta desayi","preached the seven factors of enlightenment."]],[["Te ca taṃ abhinanditvā","And they, rejoicing in that (discourse),"],["Rogā mucciṃsu taṃ khaṇe,","were freed from the illness at that very moment."],["Etena sacca vajjena","By the speaking of this truth,"],["Sotthi (te) hotu sabbadā","may you always be well!"]],[["Ekadā dhammarājāpi","Once, when the King of Dhamma (the Buddha) himself"],["Gelaññenā’bhipīḷito,","was afflicted by sickness,"],["Cundattherena taṃ yeva","He requested Venerable Cunda"],["Bhāṇāpetvāna sādaraṃ","to recite it (the Paritta) with devotion."]],[["Sammoditvāna ābādhā","Rejoicing (in the recitation), from that illness"],["Tamhā vuṭṭhāsi ṭhānāso,","He recovered instantly."],["Etena sacca vajjena","By the speaking of this truth,"],["Sotthi (te) hotu sabbadā","may you always be well!"]],[["Pahīṇāteca ābādhā","Those illnesses were eliminated"],["Tiṇṇannampi mahesinaṃ","for those three great sages,"],["Maggāhata kilesāva","like defilements destroyed by the Path,"],["Pattānuppatti dhammataṃ","attaining the state of non-arising."],["Etena sacca vajjena","By the speaking of this truth,"],["Sotthi (te) hotu sabbadā","may you always be well!"]]]}